<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:15:50Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Brazil's President Lula bans online betting ahead of presidential election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d6e71ee6feb347f4baa9a7d2051407387a23e1f2528b255a7cae09c223a8b53</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:14:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T12:36:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-president-lula-bans-online-betting-ahead-of-presidential-election--48f3127e0de1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-president-lula-bans-online-betting-ahead-of-presidential-election" /><summary type="html">Brazil’s President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva on Friday signed an order banning fixed-odds betting just over a week ahead of the first round of the presidential election, in a move he said was designed to tackle the pervasive problem of families falling into debt.</summary></entry><entry><title>CNN removed from Trump press pool despite judge order to reinstate White House access</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4285ae00456a4ab2a05d723209a3d3392a057f6c193e2c55f8ce6597f78ef34</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:15:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T05:56:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260926-cnn-removed-from-trump-press-pool-despite-judge-order-to-reinstate-white-house-access--0156d346bb62.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260926-cnn-removed-from-trump-press-pool-despite-judge-order-to-reinstate-white-house-access" /><summary type="html">US news outlet CNN has been removed from a press pool that is accompanying President Donald Trump on a trip to Tennessee on Saturday. Last week, the Trump administration barred CNN, along with MS NOW and Politico, from accessing the White House. A judge then ordered their access temporarily restored, saying the move was likely unconstitutional.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Lots of pomp but little progress as Trump and Xi end state visit to DC</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f3c3acf4691b85573a870f4135ceab90f04d7e91442146d47a08ad51b05e3b4</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T16:58:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-lots-of-pomp-but-no-progress-as-trump-and-xi-end-state-visit--18a60b896000.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-lots-of-pomp-but-no-progress-as-trump-and-xi-end-state-visit" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump and Chinese leader Xi Jinping capped a state visit to Washington on Friday with pomp and pageantry but no real breakthroughs. Trump said he discussed the Iran war with Xi during his two-day visit, with both men confirming they will meet twice more before the end of the year.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Supreme Court allows Trump to use controversial voter 'verification' system</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16029a08db055298a15ef0c3fb8e61b06abdd980c6cd31f783c10dcc3d311355</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T16:52:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-supreme-court-restores-trump-mass-voter-verification-system-despite-outcry--2eef72391964.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-supreme-court-restores-trump-mass-voter-verification-system-despite-outcry" /><summary type="html">The US Supreme Court on Friday ruled the Trump administration can use a controversial new federal database that would ostensibly verify voter citizenship in November’s elections. Critics argue the administration is exaggerating the threat of non-citizen voters – an extreme rarity in US elections – to implement policies that would disenfranchise likely Democratic voters.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump courts Xi Jinping during high-profile White House visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8d5dd77cba58d4261fd9f09df4fa2736e6517735db7b3606ac58a3c26b7040f</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T09:38:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-courts-xi-jinping-during-high-profile-white-house-visit--c7b3bc8b15d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-courts-xi-jinping-during-high-profile-white-house-visit" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump rolled out an unusually lavish welcome for Chinese President Xi Jinping, praising their personal friendship throughout a White House state dinner and other ceremonial events. While both leaders said they held frank discussions behind closed doors, the visit produced no major breakthroughs, prompting criticism from Democratic lawmakers who argued the pageantry overshadowed pressing issues including Iran, Taiwan, AI and trade.</summary></entry><entry><title>Argentina's poverty rate climbs to nearly one in three under Milei</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23055d2de952dcbb8b7e586437ad25948bef5713b9fa6ea1f5301db3a09985c0</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T02:30:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-argentina-poverty-rate-nearly-one-in-three-milei--169ea5474e26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-argentina-poverty-rate-nearly-one-in-three-milei" /><summary type="html">Argentina’s poverty rate rose to 32.3% in the first half of 2026 from 28.2% in the previous six months, official data showed on Thursday, as incomes lagged rising prices. Extreme poverty climbed to 7.5% from 6.3%. Among children aged 14 and under, 44.5% were poor.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Send in the Clowns': Viral video fuels claims Denmark trolled Trump and Rubio</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:70ca2a7ecf5b334757b89ae2a1f744f53e8e278f1cd08159fb128a9a89b97b29</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T21:00:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/send-in-the-clowns-viral-video-fuels-claims-denmark-trolled-trump-and-rubio-1--4ceb91c9c0f6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/send-in-the-clowns-viral-video-fuels-claims-denmark-trolled-trump-and-rubio-1" /><summary type="html">A viral video claims Danish officials played Judy Collins's "Send in the Clowns" as US Secretary of State Marco Rubio arrived for a Greenland signing ceremony, sparking claims of Danish "trolling". Our checks of separate livestreams confirm the song really played and the video was not manipulated. Denmark has denied choosing the music, while the UN says it did not organise the event. Whilst the song was real, there is no evidence Denmark selected it deliberately. Vedika Bahl fact-checks.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli policies threaten 'life and existence' of Palestinians, Abbas tells UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:526f554340c1cb57cd79db893f9fc600d9803dbc8868847c844dba866a723cee</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:54:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-israel-policies-threaten-life-existence-palestinian-says-abbas-un--ab406195501e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-israel-policies-threaten-life-existence-palestinian-says-abbas-un" /><summary type="html">Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas addressed the UN General Assembly on Thursday by video after being denied a visa to the United States for the second year in a row. In his prerecorded speech, he denounced Israeli policies that he said threatened Palestinians with a new Nakba and vowed that his people would remain “on their land”.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Trump views US-China relations as a personal friendship: Xi views US as an adversary to be managed'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc7d45d940685bef5ff371244af3b248b30ffa01723e972f15ff9a69978a3c58</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:01:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-views-us-china-relations-as-a-personal-friendship-xi-views-us-as-an-adversary-to-be-managed--29eaaa0e21d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-views-us-china-relations-as-a-personal-friendship-xi-views-us-as-an-adversary-to-be-managed" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Henrietta Levin, Senior Fellow with the Freeman Chair in China Studies at the Center for Strategic and International Studies in Washington. The US remains a powerful actor in its relationship with China. But power on paper is not the same thing as leverage at the negotiating table. Levin warns that President Trump’s highly personalized approach to Xi Jinping offers Beijing opportunities that China can easily exploit. Xi does not approach the relationship in the same way. Au contraire, he sees the United States as an adversary to be managed while China pursues its domestic priorities and strategic objectives in Asia, including on Taiwan.</summary></entry><entry><title>Does the future belong to China?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f677c9504884dab414e2ee1fa4676cf50421bd8ba6fc4570c64530e472f4824</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T12:32:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260924-does-the-future-belong-to-china--300d0d1807be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260924-does-the-future-belong-to-china" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump is rolling out the red carpet for his Chinese counterpart Xi Jinping ahead of Thursday's summit in Washington. But is China's leader overconfident in thinking the future belongs to Beijing? FRANCE 24's Yinka Oyetade speaks to Rex Li from King's College London.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump startled by the sound of a fighter jet</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2bf7f65c039cde114919ea3782009cb6e057e1d4bd33181a2d623299bbba1d5b</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T11:03:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-startled-by-the-sound-of-a-fighter-jet--fd5a564dc607.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-startled-by-the-sound-of-a-fighter-jet" /><summary type="html">🇺🇸 🇨🇳 As Donald #Trump welcomed his Chinese counterpart Xi #Jinping for a state visit on the tarmac of an airport near #Washington, the sound of a fighter jet during the military ceremony caught the US president off guard, prompting a series of startled facial expressions.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Death of the Soccer God' pays 'homage' to Haitian diaspora and 'those who go back &amp; do their best'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:678ad09703595069be04ef1a31848bf681474cb159ba0d227ad573a461743bf9</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T06:29:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/death-of-the-soccer-god-pays-homage-to-haitian-diaspora-and-those-who-go-back-do-their-best--5ffff12e809e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/death-of-the-soccer-god-pays-homage-to-haitian-diaspora-and-those-who-go-back-do-their-best" /><summary type="html">Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Dimitry Elias Léger, journalist and author of "Death of the Soccer God". He begins with an extraordinary but largely forgotten moment in sporting history: the Haitian-born Joe Gaetjens scoring the goal that gave the US its famous victory over England at the 1950 World Cup. But Léger is less interested in reconstructing Gaetjens’s biography than in using the football star's journey as a " jumping point" to examining diaspora, fame, mortality and moral responsibility. Success offers neither immunity from history nor escape from mortality: as he puts it, “You could be super famous and end up on death row” or die wealthy in your own bed: “Either way, you’re going to die.</summary></entry><entry><title>Politico, CNN and MS ​NOW return to White House hours after judge reorders Trump to lift ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17a99a7aa7d5e49077a49c6ae1277d76adf6224934dbf5275a11779af9d6692b</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T05:31:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-us-judge-lifts-trump-s-white-house-ban-on-cnn-ms-now-politico--9468ed6cf08e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-us-judge-lifts-trump-s-white-house-ban-on-cnn-ms-now-politico" /><summary type="html">Reporters from ​Politico, CNN and MS ​NOW were allowed to enter the ​White ‌House ⁠on ‌Thursday afternoon after being barred in the morning, despite a US federal judge ordering the reinstatement of their access. The judge then issued a second order for the Trump administration to restore the journalists' access after the media outlets called for an emergency follow-up ⁠hearing.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>France to send 'military means' to protect key Saudi oil port</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7126f44ec3b6f98d709ac72e5df7f71a3b0589248d8836f8b14d850652a7cd3f</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T03:11:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-live-netanyahu-faces-un-over-gaza-as-abbas-set-to-address-assembly-by-video--ff8dcde9286d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-live-netanyahu-faces-un-over-gaza-as-abbas-set-to-address-assembly-by-video" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron on Thursday said his country would send "military means" to protect a Saudi oil terminal from attacks by Yemen's Iran-backed Houthis. Saudi Arabia has been using the Red Sea port of Yanbu to export oil after Iran blockaded the Strait of Hormuz. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump gives Xi rare airport welcome as Chinese leader begins US state visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ad0a3a80cd89ba255ee679bfcead6f0324f2a79b3cd3bd8019d0b200da4a5a0</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T01:48:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-trump-gives-xi-rare-airport-welcome-as-chinese-leader-begins-us-state-visit--890faee8eac2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-trump-gives-xi-rare-airport-welcome-as-chinese-leader-begins-us-state-visit" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump personally welcomed Chinese President Xi Jinping at a military airfield outside Washington on Wednesday, kicking off a lavish state visit focused on trade, artificial intelligence and Iran, as the two powers seek to preserve a fragile diplomatic and economic truce.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>AI leaders urge caution at UN, with Anthropic chief pledging to slow down</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0ad974a1b05a22eee8367c9d8e7807554afc922c961b15fb23cdf8b59fa4030</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T21:46:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-ai-leaders-urge-caution-at-un-with-anthropic-chief-pledging-to-slow-down--0376a5057ab0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-ai-leaders-urge-caution-at-un-with-anthropic-chief-pledging-to-slow-down" /><summary type="html">Leaders of some of the world's biggest AI companies urged caution at the United Nations on Wednesday, warning that increasingly autonomous systems could outpace human oversight. Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei pledged to slow development to ensure new AI systems are safe, while OpenAI chief Sam Altman called for "extreme care".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Fact-checking Trump's speech at the United Nations General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e656420f47437a54c4e49d163bac878d57578fe9116e25b21f9962f6dfa7978</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T20:54:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/fact-checking-trump-s-speech-at-the-united-nations-general-assembly-1--90883f567137.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/fact-checking-trump-s-speech-at-the-united-nations-general-assembly-1" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's UN address was packed with claims that are misleading, false or exaggerated. He said the US has more munitions than it could ever use, despite reports of depleting stocks. He also claimed the US and Venezuela hold 60 percent of the world's oil, despite the numbers not adding up, and he said he had ended the war in Gaza despite ongoing Israeli strikes and deaths since last year's ceasefire. Vedika Bahl fact-checks the speech in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>No, this video doesn't disprove the 9/11 attack on the south tower of the World Trade Center</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea04bf11708af00b87543995377246a38ec533d2b6f3adf4ed9fb4a93ea03cd1</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T19:01:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-video-no-proof-plane-hit-twin-tower-9-11--3315503e2a84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-video-no-proof-plane-hit-twin-tower-9-11" /><summary type="html">A former British member of parliament implied that a video filmed from a helicopter on September 11, 2001 shows that no planes actually hit the World Trade Center's south tower, but this claim would be unfounded. The plane that hit the south tower hit the other side of the building, which isn’t visible in the video.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Disgraced Hollywood mogul Harvey Weinstein sentenced to 15 years for 2006 sex assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab054c5e375697961c9c1bdf0c2eb8cf726a14fbf3c07a1718070380f6df209b</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:55:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-disgraced-hollywood-mogul-harvey-weinstein-sentenced-to-15-years-for-2006-sex-assault--91ffc4aa930f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-disgraced-hollywood-mogul-harvey-weinstein-sentenced-to-15-years-for-2006-sex-assault" /><summary type="html">Disgraced movie mogul Harvey Weinstein was sentenced to 15 years in prison Wednesday in another #MeToo reckoning for sexually assaulting a former production assistant in 2006.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US says wants Ukraine, Russia to end strikes on energy sites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44f6259e7cdccf22e478c05503834e4ed49a88d9343ffbc753f3a096f05ffa70</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:25:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-us-says-wants-ukraine-russia-to-end-strikes-on-energy-sites-1--6a47cb7c5c74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-us-says-wants-ukraine-russia-to-end-strikes-on-energy-sites-1" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy is due to address the UN General Assembly on Wednesday, as US President Donald Trump pushes for an end to Russia’s war and Kyiv seeks to shape renewed diplomatic efforts after more than four and a half years of conflict. France 24 International affairs commentator Douglas Herbert shares further details.</summary></entry><entry><title>Zelenskyy set to address UN as Russia strikes Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f79c0b99b0446709e5324f62409c9f6cc94dd96b58bbd4ac69209f6c3585b40</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:20:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-zelenskyy-set-to-address-un-as-russia-strikes-kyiv-1--602f8dc2d515.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-zelenskyy-set-to-address-un-as-russia-strikes-kyiv-1" /><summary type="html">Russia hammered Ukraine’s capital, Kyiv, with drones in daylight attacks on Wednesday, killing two people and wounding 23, just hours before Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy was due to address world leaders at the UN General Assembly. Zelenskyy met US President Donald Trump on Tuesday, as Trump has expressed frustration over the lack of progress in talks aimed at ending the war and the continued escalation of aerial attacks by both sides. Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran’s Pezeshkian tells UN his country is ‘victim’ of US ‘terrorism’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9b07d9a21cc839eb674830c04a8d9669fbc4644073e74de87e955514bf3f814</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:57:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-s-pezeshkian-tells-un-his-country-is-victim-of-us-terrorism--68195566b037.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-s-pezeshkian-tells-un-his-country-is-victim-of-us-terrorism" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian has hit back at US President Donald Trump’s speech in his address to the UN General Assembly. He opened by showing images of Iranian civilians killed in US strikes, saying they demonstrated the impact of US and Israeli military action against Iran. During his speech, the US delegation walked out of the General Assembly hall. France 24 International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Iranian President Pezeshkian adresses UNGA</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:401d049d325012f0ffcb9c0a49e8c2a32d9d63a90ed7a68621b03f3f5b103ffd</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:44:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-iranian-president-pezeshkian-adresses-unga-1--ba655932baa6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-iranian-president-pezeshkian-adresses-unga-1" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian is speaking before the UN General Assembly Wednesday in his first speech at the world body since the US and Israel launched the conflict with his country. His address comes a day after US President Donald Trump told the UNGA he could "annihilate the Islamic Republic" and "drive them into hell".</summary></entry><entry><title>How US players are reshaping France and the continent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cc198ea9502b38539ac9ec658309903bb740f0b01bd46eb382685ba4d353ca6</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:33:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260923-how-us-players-are-reshaping-france-and-the-continent--e00e75333f5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20260923-how-us-players-are-reshaping-france-and-the-continent" /><summary type="html">In this edition we welcome CNN's correspondent in France, Melissa Bell. Melissa is the author of "Sous l'influence americaine", an investigation into American interference in France and Europe. She tells us about the ways in which American interference is being felt in Europe and France and what we should expect during the 2027 French presidential election campaign.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>Trump ramps up his war on the media</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc0d71107cba58dbcb545d272c4a51b20e01bf2f5db464b1492fbc419beebf37</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:25:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260923-trump-ramps-up-his-war-on-the-media--a04596e230e6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260923-trump-ramps-up-his-war-on-the-media" /><summary type="html">US media outlets CNN, Politico and MS NOW are suing the Trump administration after it removed their press credentials and banned them from covering the White House. FRANCE 24 spoke to Steven Herman, executive director of the Jordan Center for Journalism Advocacy and Innovation at the University of Mississippi about the legality of the move and its wider ramnifications.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>UN General Assembly to discuss war, climate and AI</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe380794f7c85d32f9afa1dc963ae1ad172a02a93932e7747739be85cbebad8c</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:20:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260923-un-general-assembly-to-discuss-war-climate-and-ai--02ea0ac4d1e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260923-un-general-assembly-to-discuss-war-climate-and-ai" /><summary type="html">World leaders are heading to New York for the world's biggest diplomatic gathering: the UN General Assembly. Throughout the week, attention will turn to the war in Iran, climate change and the race to rein in AI. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis and Theresa Squatrito from the London School of Economics discuss what to expect.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>World leaders weigh AI worries, regulations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5f6e0a884a3fd9448931d1bc7ff9159abc6afdb776e6a11263aa1416aa6271f</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:08:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/world-leaders-weigh-ai-worries-regulations--accc8fadc8ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/world-leaders-weigh-ai-worries-regulations" /><summary type="html">AI leaders are due to brief the UN Security Council at an emergency session later today. The meeting comes after weeks of warnings about the potentially uncontrollable risks posed by artificial intelligence. Delano D’Souza reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thomas Chatterton Williams on how Covid-19, George Floyd protests affected US social justice</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88c7e25bc0de323367ad8b5f7d763e47204f5fb0dcaddee4df59db778164ff94</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T12:40:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260923-thomas-chatterton-williams-on-how-covid-19-george-floyd-protests-affected-us-social-justice--8b0304083ff8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260923-thomas-chatterton-williams-on-how-covid-19-george-floyd-protests-affected-us-social-justice" /><summary type="html">An acclaimed American author has spoken to FRANCE 24 about his theories on how American society's opinion and ideas of social justice have changed since the presidency of Barack Obama. Thomas Chatterton Williams says the left became disillusioned during Obama's second term, and in later years amid the George Floyd protests and Covid-19 pandemic the discourse shifted – initially for the left, but this also impacted the right. The ripples of those times are still resonating today. His latest book is entitled "Summer of Our Discontent: The Age of Certainty and the Demise of Discourse".</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Chinese beauty products prove resilient amid US-China trade war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1733f990307f7f27c5229f61b749e21c8b605023f39c5c04d47870ca1ff7685</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T12:29:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/chinese-beauty-products-prove-resilient-amid-us-china-trade-war--12cb060c9631.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/chinese-beauty-products-prove-resilient-amid-us-china-trade-war" /><summary type="html">The US-China trade war has hit exports ranging from soybeans to solar panels, but one industry appears to be weathering the tariffs remarkably well. As Donald Trump and Xi Jinping prepare to meet in Washington this week, big-ticket exports are likely to be high on the agenda. But Chinese beauty products such as wigs, hair extensions and false eyelashes have proved highly resilient, with low prices and strong demand encouraging consumers to absorb the extra costs. China’s press-on nail industry, concentrated largely in one city, is also coming through the trade war without a scratch. Bryan Quinn</summary></entry><entry><title>Hurricane Polo churns off Mexico</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:edd5bf732873a144d19e60260757d343d5c808b26cad2117034a5a464057bbb2</id><updated>2026-09-26T13:13:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T10:49:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/hurricane-polo-churns-off-mexico--d879f74823e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/hurricane-polo-churns-off-mexico" /><summary type="html">Hurricane Polo has strengthened into one of the most powerful Pacific cyclones in decades and is expected to skirt Mexico’s southwestern coast as a Category 5 storm. The Miami-based National Hurricane Center described Polo as an “extremely dangerous” storm, with maximum sustained winds of 165 miles per hour.</summary></entry></feed>
